   "evidence": "grep over ./code for `fullInverse_mulVec`: hits only at Moments.lean:139 (its own statement) and Polynomial.lean:123/Roots.lean:52 for the distinct `_signSum`/`_tarskiQuery` names \u2014 no call site for the abstract version. Polynomial.lean:127-134 reuses `id`, `Function.injective_id`, `fullInverse_mul_fullMatrix`, `fullMatrix_mul_fullInverse`, exactly the arguments at Moments.lean:134-143.",
   "file": "TauCeti/Geometry/RealAlgebraic/SignDetermination/Polynomial.lean",
   "fix": "Derive it: `simp only [signSum_prod_pow (K := \u211a), signCount_eq_occCount]; exact fullInverse_mulVec J _`, using `signSum_prod_pow` (line 63) to convert the moment vector. This is shorter than the current proof and gives the general statement a client; the other two pairs (`mulVec_occCount` \u2192 `mulVec_signCount`, `eq_occCount` \u2192 `eq_signCount`) already follow this pattern.",
   "issue": "`fullInverse_mulVec_signSum` is the special case of `TauCeti.SignDetermination.fullInverse_mulVec` (Moments.lean:139) at `obs := fun x : Z => fun j => sign ((Q j).eval x.val)`, but it reproves it from `eq_signCount`, repeating the `columns := id` / `Function.injective_id` / `fun x => \u27e8_, rfl\u27e9` instantiation and both inverse lemmas that Moments.lean:131-143 already performed. Consequently `fullInverse_mulVec` (and `fullMatrix_mulVec_occCount`, its only client) has no consumer anywhere in the repo.",
   "line": 123
  }
